{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"import GrafluentCollections","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" imports every module. Each module also has its own documentation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and can be imported on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import GrafluentCollections","","var scores: FenwickTree = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]","print(scores.prefixSum(through: 3))  \/\/ 9","print(scores.sum(in: 2 ..< 6))       \/\/ 19"]},{"anchor":"Values-not-references","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Values, not references"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every collection is a copy-on-write struct. Assigning one copies nothing until one of the copies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is mutated; then only that copy pays, once, and the other keeps its elements:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let original: BTree = [1, 2, 3]","var copy = original","copy.insert(4)","Array(original)   \/\/ [1, 2, 3]","Array(copy)       \/\/ [1, 2, 3, 4]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices of a tree live in flat arrays linked by integer indices rather than in a class per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, so a copy is a few array copies and a traversal reads memory almost in order. The API","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"follows the standard library and Swift Collections: the sorted sets are ","type":"text"},{"code":"SetAlgebra","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"random-access collections indexed by rank, the dictionaries take ","type":"text"},{"code":"subscript(_:default:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range trees are collections of their values.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Traps-and-checked-spellings","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Traps and checked spellings"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A plain spelling traps when its precondition fails, like an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" subscript out of range: it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the fast path, for callers who know the precondition holds. Beside it, a ","type":"text"},{"code":"checked:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" spelling","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws a typed error instead, one of those in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors","type":"reference"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"try?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" turns it into an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let primes: AVLTree = [2, 3, 5, 7]","primes[2]                    \/\/ 5","try primes[checked: 9]       \/\/ throws IndexOutOfRange"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A mutation that would break a structure’s invariant, such as joining two treaps whose elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interleave, throws on its plain spelling and changes nothing. Where the standard library’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collections return an optional ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a dictionary’s subscript, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"min()"},{"type":"text","text":"), these do too."}]},{"anchor":"Grafluent-conversions","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Grafluent conversions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A collection whose shape is a tree converts to the Grafluent type of that shape: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"type":"text","text":", with an initializer on the Grafluent type that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"costs O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") once. Structures whose shape is a general graph, such as decision diagrams and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"automata, offer a view that is a Grafluent graph without copying. Either way, Grafluent’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms, drawings and file formats run over the collection; its own operations never go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the conversion. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" shows the round trip."}]},{"anchor":"Modules","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Modules"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Group","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Modules","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Search trees"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees"},{"text":" (AVL, red–black and splay trees, treaps), ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees"},{"text":" (B-trees), ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists"},{"text":" (skip lists)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/tries","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (tries over any sequence of symbols, radix and Patricia trees, Aho–Corasick automata)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Suffix structures"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/suffixstructures"},{"type":"text","text":" (suffix arrays with LCP, suffix trees, suffix automata)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Decision diagrams","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" (reduced ordered BDDs, zero-suppressed ZDDs)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Range and spatial trees"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/rangetrees","type":"reference"},{"text":" (Fenwick trees, segment trees with lazy propagation, interval trees), ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/spatialtrees","type":"reference"},{"text":" (k-d trees, quadtrees, octrees)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sequences and persistence"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/ropes","type":"reference"},{"text":" (ropes: sequences as balanced trees of chunks), ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","type":"reference"},{"text":" (path-copying weight-balanced trees that keep every version)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Caches"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/caches"},{"type":"text","text":" (LRU caches)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Shared","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"CollectionErrors","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectionErrors"}],"isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": the errors the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked:"},{"type":"text","text":" spellings throw, re-exported by every module that throws them"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluentcollections"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GrafluentCollections"}],"role":"collection","title":"GrafluentCollections","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"GrafluentCollections","symbolKind":"module"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollect